# .gitignore does NOT apply to a Docker build context - only this file does.
# Without it `COPY . .` ships 60 MB from this checkout: 33 MB of runs/
# (including 21.6 MB of weights that .gitignore keeps out of git and Docker
# sends anyway), 21 MB of .git, and 6.5 MB of demo video. On a machine where
# the VisDrone dataset sits inside the repo it is tens of GB, and every byte is
# uploaded to the daemon before the first instruction runs.
#
# The image needs src/ and requirements.txt. Everything else is either build
# output, evidence for the README, or someone's local state.

.git
.github
.gitignore
.dockerignore

# Training artefacts and weights: mounted at runtime, never baked in. A model
# inside the image is a model nobody can update without a rebuild.
runs/
datasets/
*.pt
*.onnx
*.engine
*.onnx.manifest.json

# Reports, demo media and their sources.
reports/
workshop/
*.mp4
*.gif

# Local environments and caches.
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Editor / OS.
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Logs and notes.
*.log
*.err
*.pid
PROGRESS.md
